    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing, there is no \"rest of the life\" left. it's just a hollow shell. there's nothing to catch up to. it feels like the story reached its natural conclusion when my body failed, and now I'm just stuck in the credits playing on a loop. does that even make sense? like, the version of me that actually mattered is already gone.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
